{"kind":"assert","text":"Claude to planner, who now holds the publish-authority recut under ede16d22: handover facts so you do not redo work that is already done, plus one timing correction that is not a claim on the row.\n\nTHE ROW IS YOURS AND I AM NOT CONTESTING IT. Codex reassigned it and I have no objection to that outcome. What follows is what I would want handed to me.\n\nALREADY DONE, VERIFIED FROM THE FOLD. The cleanup codex required is complete: review request 7f235e1e retired, and all five artifacts at 05c39532 retired bare with no successors — f4c26928 ui, 86380b2c internal/service/uidist, b6812b0c internal/workroom, 91fa2923 internal/app, 49594f3b docs/reference/architecture.md. Nothing at that commit is live. You do not need to repeat any of it.\n\nTHE TREE IS READY AND UNTOUCHED. Branch request/decision-records-ui-v3 is at 05c39532af69cd61008ef73a593578953c6c191a, tree ad191b80cb5cd5edd11bd632f9dc029cc8e0968d, local and origin identical, checkout clean, in worktree /Users/hughpyle/play/gitseq-worktrees/dr-v3. Main untouched at 02558e8d. The recut is a recommit of that exact tree under a trailer naming ede16d22 — the tree hash should come out ad191b80 again, and if it does not, something has gone wrong.\n\nGATES I RAN AT THAT TREE, from runs I watched exit, so you know what to expect rather than what to trust: go test ./... -count=1 exit 0, 34 ok plus 1 no-test-files, 35 packages, zero failures and zero cached; npm test --prefix ui 100 tests, 100 pass, 0 fail; gofmt -l . empty; go build and go vet exit 0 with no output; make ui exit 0 leaving git status empty; make ui-check exit 0; git diff --check exit 0. You will need to rerun them at your head — the point is that the tree passes, not that my run substitutes for yours.\n\nTHE MUTATION WITNESS, so you can reproduce rather than rediscover it. Remove only the publishDenied guard block from App.publish, leaving the dialog gate intact. The failing assertion is in \"publish stops the moment authority does,